[size=5][b]BB Tools — Bloodborne Practice Companion[/b][/size]

Set up your hunter, jump to a fight and save your favorite settings in one portable Windows app.

[b]Made with 🖤 by James Cicada.[/b]

[size=4][b]Highlights[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Build your hunter:[/b] edit Blood Echoes and attributes, heal, use infinite stamina and consumables, or adjust damage and Echoes rewards.
[*][b]Practice boss fights:[/b] revive bosses, retry encounters, travel to lamps and boss entrances, and track attempts. Includes The Old Hunters destinations.
[*][b]Find your items:[/b] spawn by ID, save favorites, or import searchable item names from your own game files.
[*][b]Make it yours:[/b] FOV up to 120°, camera adjustments, movement speed, saved presets and startup settings.
[*][b]Keep your setup:[/b] named location bookmarks, configurable hotkeys, local save backups and session logs.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Compatibility and setup[/b][/size]
[b]Bloodborne PC and shadPS4 are officially supported for CUSA03173 1.09. Tested and confirmed.[/b] Other game builds and conflicting patches are not verified. DLC destinations require the DLC installed.

[list=1]
[*]Extract the ZIP into a writable folder. The .NET runtime is included.
[*]Start the game and load your character.
[*]Run BBTools.exe, select the game/emulator process and connect. Auto-connect is available in Settings.
[/list]

Use a separate practice save for persistent edits. Camera/FOV and exploration overrides can cause visual or performance issues. The new durability repair path still needs confirmation on both hands; ending-boss revival profiles are experimental and can change story progression.

Noclip and free camera are disabled and hidden for now. Entity inspection will return with realtime targeted-enemy updates.

[size=4][b]Help improve BB Tools[/b][/size]
[b]Contributions are welcome![/b] Share bug reports, UI ideas, documentation improvements or code on [url=https://github.com/JamesCicada/bb-tools]GitHub[/url]. Include your game/runtime version, reproduction steps and relevant log when reporting a problem.

[url=https://github.com/JamesCicada/bb-tools/releases]Downloads[/url] • [url=https://github.com/JamesCicada/bb-tools/issues]Report an issue[/url] • [url=https://github.com/JamesCicada/bb-tools/blob/main/docs/COMPATIBILITY.md]Compatibility results[/url]

Free and open source under the MIT license. No game files are included. Inspired by [url=https://github.com/kh0nsu/EldenRingTool]ERTool[/url].
